  "dom_id": "step-q60566",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find $n$ such that  ${z}^{5}\\cdot {z}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{2}={z}^{n}$  is correct.",
  "worked_solution": "We add the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{5}\\cdot {z}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{2} & = \\\\ {z}^{5+7+2} & = \\\\ {z}^{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore ${z}^{n}={z}^{14}$, so $n=14.$",
